The Editor class in src/editor.ts has no undo yet. Please add undo/redo as described in docs/UNDO.md. In short, Editor gets undo(), redo(), canUndo(), canRedo() and transact(fn), and the constructor's options start being used: clock (injected so grouping is testable, default Date.now) and historyLimit (default 100, RangeError when it isn't an integer >= 0).

The parts the doc is precise about and that I care most about:
- undo and redo restore the selection as well as the text;
- consecutive single-character typing is grouped into one step while each keystroke comes less than a second after the previous one, and the doc lists exactly what counts as typing and what closes a group;
- a new change clears redo, but no-op edits and selection changes don't;
- transactions (including nested ones and ones whose callback throws);
- the history limit.

Please put the history bookkeeping in a new src/history.ts and keep editor.ts focused on editing; src/text.ts has the string and selection helpers. The existing editing behaviour of insert, deleteBackward, deleteForward and select must not change, and the Editor constructor keeps its signature (text, options).
